d students), Hair & Makeup, and Set & Prop Development.\n  - **Frame 11**: Final credits for Media & Marketing, Photography, Videography, and special acknowledgments like “Princesses” and “Iconium Strategies.”\n\nIn summary, this segment transitions from the live curtain call (Frames 1–2) into the formal closing credits (Frames 3–11), acknowledging the full cast and crew who contributed to the production of “The Little Mermaid” at Strathcona Christian Academy.'}], 'formatted_responses': ['\n=== Batch 0-11 (11 frames) ===\nFrames: /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/xECIRjlxM3U/frames/frame_7400.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/xECIRjlxM3U/frames/frame_7410.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/xECIRjlxM3U/frames/frame_7420.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/xECIRjlxM3U/frames/frame_7430.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/xECIRjlxM3U/frames/frame_7440.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/xECIRjlxM3U/frames/frame_7450.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/xECIRjlxM3U/frames/frame_7460.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/xECIRjlxM3U/frames/frame_7470.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/xECIRjlxM3U/frames/frame_7480.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/xECIRjlxM3U/frames/frame_7490.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/xECIRjlxM3U/frames/frame_7500.jpg\nVLM Response: This sequence of frames is **part of the credits/acknowledgments** at the end of the theatrical performance.\n\nHere is a detailed breakdown:\n\n- **Frame 1**: Shows the full cast on stage taking a bow under spotlights. This is the final curtain call, a traditional end to a live performance where the entire cast acknowledges the audience’s applause. This frame captures the live, celebratory moment before the credits begin.\n\n- **Frame 2**: The stage lights dim significantly, and the cast is still visible but fading into darkness. This transition signals the end of the live performance and the beginning of the closing credits se