haracters like King Triton, Sebastian, and others.\n\n- **Frame 8**: The cast begins to bow. Ariel and Eric are holding hands, taking a synchronized bow — a classic romantic finale gesture.\n\n- **Frame 9**: They rise from the bow, still holding hands, smiling at the audience. The rest of the cast is also bowing or waving.\n\n- **Frame 10**: The entire cast raises their arms in a final celebratory pose — the traditional “final bow” that signals the end of the performance. The audience (visible as silhouettes in the foreground) is likely applauding.\n\n---\n\n### **Conclusion:**\n\nThis sequence captures the **curtain call** of the “The Little Mermaid” musical production. The cast is taking their final bows, acknowledging the audience’s applause, and celebrating the successful conclusion of the show. It’s a joyful, communal moment that highlights the collaborative effort of the entire production team and cast.\n'], 'condensed_response': '**Scene Summary (Frames\u202f7300‑7390 → Curtain‑Call of *The Little\u202fMermaid* musical)**  \n\n| Frame | Characters present & key action |\n|-------|---------------------------------|\n| **7300** | The cast begins to file onto the stage. Scuttle (bird‑costume) and Prince Eric enter from opposite wings; underwater‑blue lighting washes the set. |\n| **7310** | More ensemble members line up, forming the first rows for the bow. |\n| **7320** | A figure in a chef’s hat (likely Grimsby or a towns‑folk) takes a central spot; the group starts clapping and smiling. |\n| **7330** | Ursula (black with tentacles) and other principal characters take their positions; everyone faces the audience. |\n| **7340** | Prince Eric moves to centre stage, preparing to lead the final bow; the cast arranges symmetrically. |\n| **7350** | Ariel (red‑hair, mermaid‑style dress) joins Eric at centre, the two leads ready for the joint bow. |\n| **7360** | Full ensemble in place: King Triton, Sebastian, Scuttle, Grimsby, and the chorus surround the leads. |\n| **7370** | The cast begins bowing; Ariel and Eric hold hands and bow together, a classic romantic finale gesture. |\n| **7380** | They rise, still hand‑in‑hand, while the rest of the troupe continues bowing and waving. |\n| **7390** | All performers raise their arms in a celebratory pose; spotlights highlight the cast as silhouettes of the applauding audience appear in the foreground. |\n\n**Overall:** The ten‑frame sequence captures the **curtain‑call** rather than any narrative action. Every major character—from Ariel and Prince Eric to Ursula, King Triton, Sebastian, Scuttle, and the supporting ensemble—appears together, lines up, and takes synchronized bows, culminating in a final, arms‑raised group pose that signals the end of the performance.', 'failed_images': []}}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'I need to determine the last major event in this Little Mermaid theatrical performance. Based on my previous queries, I can see that frames 7300-7500 show the curtain call and credits, which are not part of the story itself. I need to find what happens just before this - the actual final story event.\n\nLet me search for the final story scenes by looking at frames just before the curtain call. I\'ll search for frames around 7200-7300 to see what the last narrative scene might be.\n\n```json\n{\n    "tool": "VLM_QUERY",\n    "frames": ["frames/frame_7200.jpg", "frames/frame_7210.jpg", "frames/frame_7220.jpg", "frames/frame_7230.jpg", "frames/frame_7240.jpg", "frames/frame_7250.jpg", "frames/frame_7260.jpg", "frames/frame_7270.jpg", "frames/frame_7280.jpg", "frames/frame_7290.jpg"],\n    "prompt": "Describe what is happening in these frames. Is this part of the theatrical performance story? If so, describe the scene, characters, and actions. Look for any of these key events: King Triton attacking Ursula, Prince Eric kissing another woman, a wedding ceremony between Prince Eric and Ariel, or Ariel transforming into bubbles. If none of these are visible, describe what